{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159692-help-with-my-2e-character-need-help-making-or-picking-a-kith","id":1159692,"title":"Help with my 2E character, need help making or picking a kith.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-16T20:29:01-08:00","id":1159692,"title":"Help with my 2E character, need help making or picking a kith.","content":"What I propose is help developing the kith for now. None of the Kiths presented really matched what I was looking for in my Ogre. So allow me to introduce my character.<br /> Name: Will Sherman<br /> Seeming: Ogre Kith: Efreet?<br /> <br /> Will is a descendant of General Sherman. Yes that General Sherman, the one who took a long walk though Georgia. He was taken just for this. His keeper, had a sick fascination with the American Civil war. This keeper created two sides 1 side was given slaves, some of whom were other taken, or Arcadian born, and more than a few hobgoblins. They were given wealth generated by the labors of their slaves, and so on. The other side was given freedom, and better gear to wage their war with. If the North won, the south would have to relinquish their slaves and submit to the North's rules. If the South won then the northern taken would become their slaves.<br /> <br /> The taken on both sides were officers, and specialists and the generals. William was taken, and made to fill the role of an artillery piece, bringing devastation to the southern army and their fortresses. Where he and his field pieces (hobs under his direct command) things burned. Many of those things were enemy hobs, homes, and taken. <hr /><br /> So that's the relevant stuff for now. Will became an ogre by using the destructive power he had to rip, tear, and blast his way out of Arcadia under the command of General Josephine Grant. So...kith ideas.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">My first idea is that the skill of choice is Science.<br /> An Efreet who uses science to determine the weak point of a none living object (Like a building or car) gains an exceptional success at 3 successes rather than 5<br /> <br /> For power...I cam up with this.<br /> Explosive Blast: The Efreet can channel fire, made from their passion and rage. By spending a Glamour for the scene they may bring forth their flames allowing them to launch a ranged attack with one hand. Launching a torrent of flames with little care for accuracy only purging their foes by flame. This effectively turns their hand into a flame thrower for the scene. They may make a ranged attack with a dice pool of Strength + Athletics - Defense. For an additional will power and ending the effect, the Efreet may choose instead to use both hands and throw a single explosive fireball. This fireball it treated like a Grenade (see hurt locker) with the following stats Damage [Wyrd], Blast Radius [Stamina x2], Force [Strength].<br /> <br /> Efreet are made by their keepers to be engines of destruction and shock weapons. The goal of their creation is often war with a neighboring gentry who's story threatens to spill into theirs. These weapons exist to sow fear, and devastation in their wake.<br /> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-17-2017, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T02:16:32-08:00","id":1159751,"title":"","content":"Okay revised version. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Efreet</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It is the screams of the children I remember most. The smell of cooked human flesh is exactly like that of pork. I remember them, their faces as they burned, as they screamed and begged for mercy. It is something that haunts me every time. How do I deal with it? For starters...I don\u2019t eat pork.</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes the gentry just need to quell a rebellion, destroy a neighbor, or incinerate a hobgoblin village. When they need such an engine of destruction they make an Efreet. These power houses are made from those who have strong burning tempers, not always ones that explode fast but that can build up over time into raging infernos. A passionate personality is required as well. These changelings become avatars of carnage, and flame and when set loose upon their targets leave only ash in their wake.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fairest: An exotic muscular figure with reddish skin and small horns, who when exited or angered seems to be aglow from within.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ogre: A beastial figure of claws, rage, horns, and flame. It\u2019s face that of a predator, and yet very expressive almost human.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When using Craft to demolish a building or other inanimate object, an exceptional success is gained on 3 successes instead of the usual 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Burning Wrath - By spending a point of glamor for the scene the efreet may channel their rage and passion into a torrent flames that they may project as a short, medium, or long burst attack. This attack is mirrors a burst from a military flame thrower and should be thought of as such, it has the incendiary tag but uses athletics + dexterity instead of firearms, and does not require a speciality. The short burst attack may be used without penalty and simulates a narrow short cone of flames, the medium burst attack causes the efreet to lose their defense in close combat as they are more focused on their attack to noticed anyone attacking at melee range representing a wall of flame similar to a medium burst from a flame thrower, the long burst adds that they cannot move before or while firing this is a long burst from a flame thrower a great jet of flames that risks knocking an unbraced efreet onto their back. The Efreet may choose to end the effect early by spending a willpower and creating an explosive fireball. This fireball may be thrown as per grenade rules and has the same range as an aerodynamic thrown weapon. Damage value for both modes of attack is equal to least of wyrd or 5. The explosion has a blast radius of 2x stamina and a force of strength. The damage of the flame torrent is the maximum damage it can do to any one target.<br /> <br /> edit: updated as per MCN's statement that rules may not be obvious or defined well enough.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-22-2017, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T03:26:51-08:00","id":1159762,"title":"","content":"Hrm.... so, I'm just going to ramble here and talk about potential points you might want to consider. Take or leave the advice as you wish.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're trying to make the elemental warrior FS* as a kith to a greater or lesser extent. Or, at least something along those lines. In either case, comparing the two, we can see that the EWFS lists distances and dice pools. You have neither listed in the second, and only a dice pool in the first. Kind of necessary for this kind of ability. Also, if we're doing fire, we should talk about Size and Intensity of flames, and how it might spread.<br /> <br /> There also be overlap not only with the EWFS merit, but Elemental Weapon (Whatever that is) or one of the Elemental Contracts. We haven't seen any contracts beyond Autumn and Steed, so its entirely possible that your kith will be rendered redundant, make Contracts meaningless, or be overshadowed entirely by new stuff. Something to keep in mind in the coming weeks.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not seeing the connection between the skill and the ability. The former is about studious study and precision when dismantling something. A surgical strike, if you will. The latter is just filling the air with &quot;flame bullets.&quot; There's no synergy between them at all, nothing to tie them together other than &quot;destruction&quot; as a vague concept. I suggest tightening the concept a bit if you want to go that route. <br /> <br /> Underhill changeling focused less on getting lots of weapon modifiers, and more on giving 'lings massive dice pools in terms of combat abilities. A measure of that still exists with pledges, which can give large dice pools. Same with Steed Contracts to an extent - we may have the potential for agg claws, but no +X damage rating. Just something to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> * <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/merits-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/merits-changeling-the-lost/</a> for reference if you need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T04:00:31-08:00","id":1159768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159692-help-with-my-2e-character-need-help-making-or-picking-a-kith?p=1159762#post1159762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm.... so, I'm just going to ramble here and talk about potential points you might want to consider. Take or leave the advice as you wish.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're trying to make the elemental warrior FS* as a kith to a greater or lesser extent. Or, at least something along those lines. In either case, comparing the two, we can see that the EWFS lists distances and dice pools. You have neither listed in the second, and only a dice pool in the first. Kind of necessary for this kind of ability. Also, if we're doing fire, we should talk about Size and Intensity of flames, and how it might spread.<br /> <br /> There also be overlap not only with the EWFS merit, but Elemental Weapon (Whatever that is) or one of the Elemental Contracts. We haven't seen any contracts beyond Autumn and Steed, so its entirely possible that your kith will be rendered redundant, make Contracts meaningless, or be overshadowed entirely by new stuff. Something to keep in mind in the coming weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops thank you. For pointing that out an earlier version listed that range was same as flame thrower. The second mode does have a range listed. As per grenade. That's throwing distance. I edited the version above to call out that range and rules follow military flame thrower and as such damage is the max damage it can do. Also re-edited it to list dice pool for this attack as it is in exception to the normal flame thrower rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159692-help-with-my-2e-character-need-help-making-or-picking-a-kith?p=1159762#post1159762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not seeing the connection between the skill and the ability. The former is about studious study and precision when dismantling something. A surgical strike, if you will. The latter is just filling the air with &quot;flame bullets.&quot; There's no synergy between them at all, nothing to tie them together other than &quot;destruction&quot; as a vague concept. I suggest tightening the concept a bit if you want to go that route.<br /> <br /> Underhill changeling focused less on getting lots of weapon modifiers, and more on giving 'lings massive dice pools in terms of combat abilities. A measure of that still exists with pledges, which can give large dice pools. Same with Steed Contracts to an extent - we may have the potential for agg claws, but no +X damage rating. Just something to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> * <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/merits-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/merits-changeling-the-lost/</a> for reference if you need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The skill is about imploding a building, or blowing something up with a detonation. The power is about causing a detonation which can implode a building, blow up an object, or burn clear a fortifaction. The idea here is that the user becomes a living analog to a cannon, long tom, or howitzer (only with a severely crippled range by comparison because let's face it having a range great enough to hit a target in another city would be broken as hell).<br /> <br /> Using that knowledge of what I'm going for, would you say that is still fitting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-17-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T04:48:18-08:00","id":1159780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159692-help-with-my-2e-character-need-help-making-or-picking-a-kith?p=1159762#post1159762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not seeing the connection between the skill and the ability. The former is about studious study and precision when dismantling something. A surgical strike, if you will. The latter is just filling the air with &quot;flame bullets.&quot; There's no synergy between them at all, nothing to tie them together other than &quot;destruction&quot; as a vague concept. I suggest tightening the concept a bit if you want to go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per Hurt Locker. Crafts is about taking a knife to a brake line to wreck a car. but you are right. The fitting skill would be the one used to place a bomb in a building and bring the whole thing down. Or better analogy knowing where to aim a artillery round to take down a building. I could have sworn that was crafts. Remember the torrents of flame are there to soften the target, create an opening, or burn out defenders before blowing it up. So any suggestions on an alternate skill would be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-17-2017, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:21:59-08:00","id":1159832,"title":"","content":"Well, here's how I think about it. Kiths grant you a specialty, just a different bonus instead of +1 dice. So, here's the question I think we should be asking. What skills will your bob-omb be using in the course of play? The specialty is going to be &quot;destroying things,&quot; but how is that going to be done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:29:07-08:00","id":1159836,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> Well I would assume Intimidation, and crafts (to demolish buildings, cars, statues the like). But also persuasion, and expression, and brawl. Will isn't a bad person, rough around the edges, but he has his gentle side. Particular soft spot for small children whom he feels he needs to protect. Very strong big brother complex with him.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs to how he will be destroying things...but blowing them into the air, into pieces or heating them up till the point the metal becomes too soft to support the weight and collapse naturally. Blowing something up and over a bit not only destroys it but can be useful for simultaneously creating road blocks and traffic hazards to help friends escape. Of course just simply turning it into slag and rubble is also useful. But a slow destruction from weakened supports gives me and my motley plenty of time to escape. All ways to destroy something that I mentioned are helpful and beneficial (to us). I will also add, that if you need inspiration on what can be done with exposives there is a TV show to watch called Burn Notice. Keep your eye on Fiona Glennanne. She can work wonders with a block of c4 and very little prep time that are examples of crafting awesome and making use of what's in Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> Edit: Amended for further clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-17-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T00:52:28-08:00","id":1161446,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t heard back from @MCN in a few days. Every thing okay? Do I need to provide more information about the character or the inspiration? In case you aren\u2019t familiar with one of the most famous Generals of the American Civil War <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Tecumseh_Sherman\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will...cumseh_Sherman</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T04:01:33-08:00","id":1161468,"title":"","content":"Sorry, got distracted by shiny things. <br /> <br /> Anyways, with the new preview out, I'm going to have to say that the earlier worries about damage is kinda redundant - Elemental weapon puts that idea to bed rather firmly. Elemental weapon can only make archaic weapons, nothing resembling a gun. So, no overlap there.<br /> <br /> In terms of the skill, you're right that Crafts is the best one, but I think the problem I really ran into is that you're talking about <u><b>planning</b></u>destruction, instead of actually doing said destruction. So, a rewording to have the exceptional on three for using crafts to damage or destroy things, rather than just executing planning. This makes it a bit more in theme with how I feel the kith shapes up, actually broadens the ways you can use the skill without removing any of the old as well, and it synergies with some other abilities in the new book. All in all, a solid specialty that's likely to come up in play with how your kith functions, at least I think it would.<br /> <br /> That's my recommendation, at least. Again, sorry for the wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T05:59:24-08:00","id":1161486,"title":"","content":"No big deal. I thought you might be waiting for this preview after a day or two went by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}